  "summary": "Lint, tests (145) and build all pass.\n\n**Item 14 — UC2 contract document generation.** The actual document generation (merge-field fill from the template, or taking the uploaded third-party file as-is, and storing it as Version 1) happens on the backend's `POST /api/v1/contracts`. In `src/pages/NewContractPage.jsx` the confirmation existed but was unreachable: `setSuccessMessage(...)` was immediately followed by `navigate()`, so the page unmounted before the banner rendered. The success banner now stays on screen showing \"Contract created successfully and saved as Draft\" plus which source produced Version 1 (template merge vs. uploaded third-party paper, no merge), with a **View Contract** button that performs the navigation.\n\n**Item 3 — UC5 re-check risk after external changes.** Re-scoring itself is backend work. Added `src/features/negotiation/components/RiskRecheckPanel.jsx`, rendered from `NegotiationTrackerPage` whenever the latest version's `source` is `External`. It uses only existing contract endpoints: `GET .../negotiation/compare` to identify the clauses the counterparty actually changed, and `GET .../clause-analysis` for the refreshed scores — listing a new risk score only for changed clauses and showing the updated overall score. When `analysisStatus === 'Failed'` it states that the external version is still saved and previous scores are unchanged, and offers a **Retry Risk Analysis** button wired to `POST .../retry-extraction`.\n\nReading taken: the smaller one — both items' generation/re-scoring logic belongs to the backend repository, so I implemented only the frontend surfacing of their results, inventing no new paths or fields.",
